; bluefin-gdx-swtpm.cil — let swtpm write its per-VM log.
;
; On a normal RPM install the swtpm-tools package ships /var/log/swtpm and the
; swtpm domain can write the per-VM TPM log there. On this bootc/ostree image
; that path is recreated at runtime (see tmpfiles.d/bluefin-gdx-swtpm.conf) and
; ends up labeled virt_log_t — which swtpm_t is NOT granted write on by the
; policy shipped in this base. The result is swtpm_setup dying on launch with the
; misleading "swtpm at /usr/bin/swtpm does not support TPM 2" (it's really
; "couldn't open my log file"), which fails every TPM-2.0 VM start.
;
; This restores the one missing allow. Loaded at build time with
; `semodule -X 300 -i` (see the recipe), the bootc-supported way to ship a
; policy module so it persists on the deployed system.
(allow swtpm_t virt_log_t (file (getattr open read append write ioctl)))
